      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{3x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{1}{3x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{3x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/82fe9722e04ff16c6fea7ca10988dfa8e581c0cf341f7bde82fdec5ff21b5df9.png)",
