      "dom_id": "step-q113466",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{x-2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{2}{x-2},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/9da0db2e6c97e507e82b7ca801e46802fabf91ad31ff53ad3cc9ae580151370a.png)\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/3c8dd0e4726747b00e4377e43c06693326e10db2977257c9c20da4953127ddfd.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{x-2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/207dec9757b65a75c25ba7ace7a12bec8e922bda9018e58d6511d12de47426b7.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
